From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:04:59 +0200
Subject: net: lantiq: cbm: remove the datapath registry the buffer manager
 exported

The buffer manager published a small registry to the rest of the vendor
suite: allocate a datapath port, enable it, look its dequeue resources
up, hand its queue-index-table rows out, take it back again. It was
reached from the switch API and the datapath registry, both of which are
gone, and from an ioctl surface that went with them.

None of it has a caller now, and none of it is what the manager's own
probe uses - the probe reads the same tables directly. Remove the port
allocator and its enable hook, the six list and lookup helpers left
behind them, and the two enqueue and dequeue wrappers the ioctl surface
called.

That empties the file the port allocator lived in, and empties the last
reason for a header in the global include path: it declared eighteen
functions for one translation unit inside this driver, and every one of
them is now either removed or local.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

